&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community you will join&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb’s Design Operations team ensures the Design organization runs effectively and at scale, enabling teams to deliver products that are usable, lovable, and globally impactful. This team partners closely with Design, Product Management, Engineering, Marketing, Creative and business leaders, fostering strong alignment and seamless day-to-day operations. The environment is highly collaborative, fast-moving, and focused on scaling design impact through operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Senior Design Program Manager, you will drive the end-to-end program management of a design team focused on delivering critical product initiatives. You will scope, plan, execute, and launch programs that directly impact Airbnb’s hosts and guests while aligning closely with roadmap commitments. Success in this role means ensuring cross-functional alignment, proactively managing risks, and driving operational consistency that enables Design to deliver measurable outcomes at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Design Managers, Directors, and cross-functional leaders to align on program scope, timelines, goals and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish operating rhythms across design teams, including communication cadences, resource planning, and leadership check-ins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the planning and execution of quarterly and annual product launches, ensuring design workstreams are delivered with quality and on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the bridge across Design, Engineering, Product Marketing, Business teams and other key cross-functional partners, ensuring visibility, communication, and risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate and resolve obstacles across teams, proactively elevating risks and implementing solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold design standards and best practices by driving consistent adoption of the design process &amp;amp; tools and continuously refining workflows to improve quality and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in Consulting, Program Management, Product/Project Management, or related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage and deliver impactful design initiatives in large digital product organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record in navigating ambiguity, structuring solutions, and driving initiatives from conception through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic mindset with the ability to balance long-term thinking with near-term execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership in mediation, negotiation, and conflict resolution, with the ability to influence senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing systems and scalable processes where little exists, with a flexible, solutions-oriented mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for organizational excellence, detail orientation, and thriving in a fast-paced, hyper-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep appreciation for the Product Design process and experience working within cross-functional, product-driven organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Homes team grows Airbnb&#39;s destination business. We manage a competitive portfolio of accommodations that meets guest expectations for value, variety, and quality. We help all types of hosts grow their business through new products, partnerships, best practices, and innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will take full ownership of growing Airbnb&#39;s destination business in Thailand and Vietnam. You will lead your team to partner with top local hosts to improve host quality, optimize listings, and grow account performance. You will design and execute local initiatives that grow high-value inventory and support host success across every segment. You will work in close partnership with Global Markets, Product, Legal, Policy, Communications, and Marketing to drive sustainable growth for Airbnb in the country.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive destination strategies to scale the local business across target cities in Thailand and Vietnam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, motivate, and coach a team of Market Managers to grow Airbnb&#39;s Homes and Hotels business in Thailand and Vietnam through effective account management and key country initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Localize global and regional strategies to fit local nuances, including consumer behavior, regulations, and competitive dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead acquisition strategy and host onboarding programs to continuously diversify the portfolio of accommodations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboard and manage partners, and optimize their listings to drive engagement and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with key accounts, evaluate growth opportunities, and lead joint initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and oversee host engagement at scale, including programs, campaigns, and communications that reach hosts across target cities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional teams to drive adoption of new products and initiatives that improve listing quality, host engagement, and market share.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify market trends and opportunities, and provide solutions to overcome barriers and capitalize on emerging demand or regulatory shifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Airbnb at external speaking events, industry forums, and partner gatherings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach team members to reach their full potential in their current role while developing them for future roles within the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in commercial roles, strategy, global operations, business development, or marketplace management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years managing teams, with a track record of growing and scaling high-performing organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in travel technology and consulting is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluency in English and at least one local language (Thai or Vietnamese).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and strategic skills, using data to uncover opportunities, shape portfolio strategy, and guide market decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A blend of operational and commercial skills to acquire supply across multiple channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence product, policy, and cross-functional teams to unlock new revenue and improve host and market performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with dashboards and analytics tools to drive team and individual performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success achieving results through others, including performance management and team building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bold, compassionate leader who gives clear direction, constructive feedback, and hands-on coaching, and who builds an inclusive, high-performing culture in close partnership with regional and global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized, able to run multiple initiatives at once and turn strategy into results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

